<title>UK: Baltic Freight Index rose two points to 1,281.</title>
<headline>Baltic Freight Index rose two points to 1,281.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index for spot dry cargo shipping rates rose to 1,281 today from 1,279 on May 12, with the base being Jan 4 1985 equals 1,000. The BFI is based on the following sub-indices with rates</p>
<p>in dollars per tonne.</p>
<p> Route Index     Rate   Prev Index  Rate</p>
<p>   1    1360    12.350	  1360    12.350</p>
<p>   1a   1297  9825.000	  1292  9788.000</p>
<p>   2    1523    21.763	  1522    21.750</p>
<p>   2a   1545 12669.000	  1532 12563.000</p>
<p>   3    1363    12.575	  1362    12.563</p>
<p>   3a   1177  9288.000	  1170  9238.000</p>
<p>   6    1213    12.513	  1217    12.556</p>
<p>   7    1148     5.588	  1151     5.606</p>
<p>   8     874     9.613	   876     9.638</p>
<p>   9     726  6350.000	   721  6306.000</p>
<p>  10    1105     5.581	  1106     5.588</p>
